    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d22-a4">

                <pb facs="0138" n="42" sameAs="frus:frus1872p1/pg42"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">transandine telegraph.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Buenos
                                Ayres, Hotel Paix</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1872-07-26"><hi rendition="#italic">July</hi> 26,
                        1872</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Sir</hi>: While I hear the booming of guns,
                    the ringing of bells, and the rejoicing of multitudes on this eventful day,
                    allow me to offer you my warmest congratulations that your great enterprise has
                    been crowned with success; that the populations of the east and west are thus
                    brought together; that the formidable barrier of the Andes has thus been
                    overcome, and this republic will owe you an eternal debt of gratitude for this
                    immense boon you have just conferred upon them.</p>
                <p>Accept my best wishes.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>W. WHEELWRIGHT.</signed>
                </closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">J. Clark</hi>, Esq.</p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
